  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nCAA regime is in place across the Ohio Valley. Satellite imagery \nshowing some breaks in the clouds that will allow for weak \ninstability to develop this afternoon. Combined with the \nnorthwesterly flow regime, spotty showers are expected today. Shower\ncoverage will decrease this evening with the loss of diurnal \nheating, but renewed chances are expected tonight as a shortwave \nswings through. \n\nSynoptic pattern remains fairly unchanged on Friday. As a result,\nsimilar conditions are expected: Seasonably cool temperatures, breezy\nnorthwesterly winds, and mostly cloudy skies with spotty showers. The\ncolumn of air aloft will be cooler on Friday compared to today, so\nthermal profiles may support some snowflakes reaching the surface. \n\nSurface high pressure does eventually take hold of the Ohio Valley\nthis weekend, which will end the chances for pcpn. However, the cooler\nair mass remains intact, keeping high temps in the 40s through this \nweekend.",
